{# MODULES IN THIS AREA — which are switched on here, and the way into each.

   THE REGISTRY'S OWN CELL, and the only one on this page that is about the
   composition rather than about the ground. It states what the area runs
   against what the installation HAS, because "three modules" means nothing
   without "of nine": an area is deliberately narrower than the catalogue.

   EVERY ROW IS A MODULE'S ENTRY ROUTE, resolved live from its provider, so
   uninstalling one takes its row with it rather than leaving a dead link. #}
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">Modules in this area<span class="src">&middot; {{ moduleCards|length }} installed &middot; {{ catalogueCount }} in the catalogue</span></span>
    <span class="ao-by next"><i></i>the registry</span>

    {% if moduleCards is empty %}
        {# NOT INSTALLED HERE — the honest-absent state, and it names the
           three contributions this page is waiting for rather than drawing
           them empty. Nothing here is invented, because there is nothing. #}
        <div class="use" style="margin:0 2px 12px"><b>Not installed in this area.</b>
            Nothing here is drawn with invented data, because there is none.
            An area with no modules is new, not broken: this page is the frame every module's
            contribution lands in, and it is empty until one is switched on.</div>
        <div class="ao-slot">
            <div class="ao-slotrow">
                <span class="nm">Right now</span>
                <span class="wd">A tile per module with something happening this minute, in that module&rsquo;s own words.</span>
                <span class="st">awaiting a module</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ao-slotrow">
                <span class="nm">Needs attention</span>
                <span class="wd">A row per thing a module says somebody has to act on, sorted by urgency across all of them.</span>
                <span class="st">awaiting a module</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ao-slotrow">
                <span class="nm">Map layers</span>
                <span class="wd">The plate already draws the area&rsquo;s boundary and zones; each module adds the data it owns as its own layer.</span>
                <span class="st">awaiting a module</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        {% if is_granted('module.view') %}
            <div class="rln" style="margin-top:12px">
                <span class="fog">Switch one on</span>
                <span class="mono acc" style="font-size:11px"><a href="{{ path('area_modules', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">the Modules tab &rarr;</a></span>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    {% else %}
        <div class="ao-slot">
            {% for module in moduleCards %}
                <div class="ao-slotrow">
                    <span class="nm">{{ module.title }}</span>
                    <span class="wd">{{ module.source ?? 'reads what it records in this area' }}</span>
                    <span class="st">
                        {%- if module.url %}<a class="more" href="{{ module.url }}">Open &rarr;</a>
                        {%- else %}{{ module.status }}{% endif -%}
                    </span>
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
